# The hal stops (console "stop", or a fault that stops the hal) while the
# drive is enabled: the F4's io rt_stop drops DIO0 so the holding brake
# grips. Before 2026-11-10 io4 had no rt_stop and PE4 kept its last level,
# so the brake stayed released with the outputs off (DEBUGNOTES).
# host/hw/io.c mirrors io4 (out0_state = what PE4 drives); tests/
# check_safety_wiring.py checks that io4's rt_stop really drives PE4 low.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 60
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
io0.out0_state
stop
run 0.1
io0.out0_state
@expect io0.out0_state[1] == 1
@expect io0.out0_state[2] == 0
